rowly tailored to prevent undue\nmarket influence by identifying select parcels using metes and bounds\ndescriptions. A licensee can only make use of this kind of exemption if\neach of its New York-based alcohol manufacturing, wholesale and retail\nbusiness parcels are exempted.\n\nThis bill's exemption will assist with the economic revitalization of a\ndistressed area in the City of Troy, namely Census Tract 404, which has\nan estimated per capita income of less than $14,000 and where an esti-\nmated 48% of its approximately 2,200 residents live below the poverty\nline. The property, which is listed on the National Historical Register,\nwill be developed for mixed-use and will include a brewery and restau-\nrant. The business operation will generate fifty new jobs and increase\nsales, excise and property tax revenue.  Redeveloping the property will\nalso help fulfill the City of Troy's important historic preservation\ngoals.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nDevelopment of an affected parcel in City of Troy, County of Rensselaer,\nwill help generate sales, excise and property tax revenue.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis legislation will take effect immediately.\n",
